nt / antihypertensive"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"glipiZIDE / glyBURIDE"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Two different sulfonylureas"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"cycloSPORINE / cycloSERINE"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Immunosuppressant / antibiotic"}]]}],["$","tr","6",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"vinBLAStine / vinCRIStine"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Two chemotherapy agents — a fatal confusion"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Look-alike / sound-alike pairs to know"}]]}]
17:["$","div","2",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"The capital letters in that table are tall man lettering, and they are not a typographic quirk. Emphasizing the differing portion of two similar names measurably reduces selection errors, and it appears on labels, shelf tags, and ordering systems for exactly that reason. When you see it, it is telling you that this name has a dangerous twin."]}]
18:["$","figure","3",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Check"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"When"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Read the label at the shelf"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Before picking up the bottle"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Read it again when counting"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"As the tablets go into the tray"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Read it again at the point of labelling"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Before the label is applied"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Match the NDC number, not the name"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Numbers do not look alike the way names do"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Check the strength as carefully as the name"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Right drug, wrong strength is equally an error"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Never rely on bottle appearance"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Manufacturers change packaging without notice"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"The checks that catch a selection error"}]]}]
19:["$","div","4",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"If you discover a dispensing error after the medication has left, report it immediately to the pharmacist — do not attempt to correct it yourself and do not delay while deciding how to phrase it. The patient may need to be contacted before the next dose. Pharmacies have error reporting processes precisely because errors happen to careful people, and the purpose is to fix the system rather than to blame the person. Concealing one converts a mistake into something far more serious."]}]
1a:["$","$L1e","5",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"What is the most reliable way to confirm you have pulled the correct product?","options":["Recognizing the bottle, since you handle it daily","Matching the NDC number on the stock bottle to the one on the prescription record","Checking that the name starts with the same letters","Confirming it is in the correct position on the shelf"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"NDC numbers are unique to the product, strength, and package size, and unlike names they do not look alike. Matching the number catches both a wrong-drug and a wrong-strength selection, which name-checking alone may not.","optionRationales":["Manufacturers change packaging without notice, and familiarity is exactly what fails on a busy shift.","Correct. The NDC is unique and unambiguous.","Matching first letters is how hydralazine and hydroxyzine get confused in the first place.","Shelf position is useful but items get misplaced, and it confirms nothing about strength."]}}]
1b:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Learn the pairs cold. This is the part of the job where errors reach patients."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find the ISMP list of confused drug names and select ten pairs relevant to a retail setting. Learn what each drug is for."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"For each pair, write one sentence on what would happen if a patient received the wrong one."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Research tall man lettering and find three real examples of it on labels or in a formulary."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write out the steps you would take, in order, on discovering a dispensing error after the patient has left."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
